§ `VerifyDeadBranchFixture`

-- Negative control: an OR limb that cannot hold in the context that reaches it.
--
-- `L4.Transform.simplify` puts the ladder body in CONJUNCTIVE normal form, so
-- this reads as two clauses. Inside the second, the `NOT x` limb is dead,
-- because the first clause already requires `x`. The rule means exactly
-- `x AND y` and says so the long way.
--
-- The inner parentheses around `NOT x` are load-bearing: NOT binds LOOSER than
-- OR here, so `NOT x OR y` parses as `NOT (x OR y)` and the fixture becomes an
-- `unsat` (which is a different finding, and was what this file measured until
-- the parentheses went in).

GIVEN x IS A BOOLEAN
      y IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `one limb is inoperative` IS
  x AND ((NOT x) OR y)
